===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|dwóh₁}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|wode}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wudu}}, {{m|ang|widu||wood, forest, grove; tree; timber}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*widu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*widuz||wood}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁weydʰh₁-||to separate}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|wede|t=wood, twig}}, {{cog|gmh|wite|t=wood}}, {{cog|da|ved|t=wood}}, {{cog|sv|ved|t=firewood}}, {{cog|is|viður|t=wood}}. Further cognates include {{cog|ga|fiodh||t=a wood, tree}}, {{cog|ga|fid||t=tree}} and {{cog|cy|gwŷdd||t=trees}}; all from {{der|en|cel-pro|*widus||t=wood}}. Unrelated to {{noncog|nl|woud|t=forest}}, {{noncog|de|Wald|t=forest}} (see {{noncog|en|wold}}).

