* {{rhymes|en|ʊd|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|would}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The substance making up the central part of the [[trunk]] and [[branches]] of a [[tree]]. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.
#: {{ux|en|This table is made of '''wood'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|There was lots of '''wood''' on the beach.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=X|lines=1006–11|passage=O that men&nbsp;/ (Canſt thou believe&#8239;?) ſhould be ſo ſtupid grown,&nbsp;/ While yet the Patriark liv’d, who ſcap’d the Flood,&nbsp;/ As to forſake the living God, and fall&nbsp;/ To worſhip thir own work in '''Wood''' and Stone&nbsp;/ For Gods&#8239;!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author=w:Margery Allingham| title=w:The China Governess| chapter=Foreword| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W| passage=He stood transfixed before the unaccustomed view of London at night time, a vast panorama which reminded him [&hellip;] of some '''wood''' engravings far off and magical, in a printshop in his childhood.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The wood of a particular species of tree.
#: {{ux|en|Teak is much used for outdoor benches, but a number of other '''woods''' are also suitable, such as ipé, redwood, etc.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Walls and Ceilings|editor=Robert M. Jones|ISBN=0809434520| year=1980| publisher=Time-Life Books| page=93| passage=A few '''woods''', such as cedar and redwood, are prized for their rugged naturalness and they age so beautifully that they are generally left unfinished.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|often|as [[plurale tantum]]}} A forested or [[wooded]] area.
#: {{synonyms|en|woods|forest|woodland|Thesaurus:forest}}
#: {{ux|en|A '''wood''' beyond this moor was viewed as a border area in the seventeenth century.}}
#: {{ux|en|He got lost in the '''woods''' beyond Seattle.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|act=IV|scene=i|page=144|column=2|lines=92–94|passage=''Macbeth'' ſhall neuer vanquiſh’d be, vntill&nbsp;/ Great Byrnam '''Wood''', to high Dunſmane Hill&nbsp;/ Shall come againſt him.}}
# [[firewood|Firewood]].
#: {{ux|en|We need more '''wood''' for the fire.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|author=w:Joseph C. Lincoln|chapter=8
|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5535161W Mr. Pratt's Patients]
|passage=We toted in the '''wood''' and got the fire going nice and comfortable. Lord James still set in one of the chairs and Applegate had cabbaged the other and was hugging the stove.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=w:Henry Petroski
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/geothermal-energy Geothermal Energy]
|volume=101|issue=4|magazine=w:American Scientist
|passage=Energy has seldom been found where we need it when we want it. Ancient nomads, wishing to ward off the evening chill and enjoy a meal around a campfire, had to collect '''wood''' and then spend time and effort coaxing the heat of friction out from between sticks to kindle a flame.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|golf}} A type of [[golf club]], the [[head]] of which was traditionally made of wood.
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[woodwind]] instrument.
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang}} An [[erection]] of the [[penis]].
#: {{ux|en|That girl at the strip club gave me '''wood'''.}}
# {{lb|en|chess|uncountable|slang}} Chess pieces.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1971|title=Chess Life & Review|volume=26|page=309
|passage={{...}} White has nothing but a lot of frozen '''wood''' on the board while Black operates on the Q-side.}}

=====Usage notes=====
In the sense of "a forested area", the singular generally refers to a discrete area of forest, while the plural is often used when a more vaguely defined area is meant.

